# Pairs with ReconcileDeletesOnlyDeleted. Recovery is assumed to bring back every key
# written before the soft delete. A recovery that loses a key without re-stamping the
# lineage token leaves an absence the gates cannot tell from a delete.
MODULE: ReconcileDeletesOnlyDeletedRecoverLosesKeys
TARGET: ReconcileDeletesOnlyDeleted
CLASS: Invariant
SUMMARY: recovery loses keys without re-stamping the lineage, so their absence is reconciled as a delete
PERTURBS: Recover

--- FIND
    /\ deleted' = FALSE
    /\ UNCHANGED <<authored, wal, cursor, reg, clk,
--- REPLACE
\* MUTATION: recovery loses the key.
    /\ deleted' = FALSE
    /\ reg' = [reg EXCEPT ![s] = Absent]
    /\ UNCHANGED <<authored, wal, cursor, clk,
--- END
